%% The life of one order, end to end. Render with https://mermaid.live or the Mermaid CLI.
%% The two things this diagram exists to show:
%%   1. the 201 is returned before anything is published - the outbox is the durability boundary
%%   2. the fill comes back to order-service over Kafka, not as a return value
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client
    participant GW as api-gateway
    participant OS as order-service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant K as Kafka
    participant ME as matching-engine
    participant PS as position-service

    C->>GW: POST /api/v1/orders (Bearer JWT)
    GW->>GW: verify RS256 + rate limit per account
    GW->>OS: proxied request

    OS->>OS: bean validation
    OS->>OS: instrument lookup (Redis-cached)
    OS->>OS: 3 pre-trade risk checks

    rect rgba(130,170,255,0.12)
        note over OS,DB: one transaction
        OS->>DB: INSERT order (NEW to VALIDATED)
        OS->>DB: INSERT order_audit
        OS->>DB: INSERT outbox
    end

    OS-->>C: 201 Created
    note right of OS: durable, not yet published

    loop outbox poller
        OS->>DB: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        OS->>K: orders.accepted.v1 (key = symbol)
        OS->>DB: mark published
    end

    K->>ME: partition for this symbol (single consumer thread)
    ME->>ME: match against in-memory price-time book
    ME->>ME: tradeId = f(symbol, sequence) - deterministic
    ME->>K: trades.executed.v1

    par order-service applies its own fill
        K->>OS: trades.executed.v1
        OS->>DB: INSERT order_fill PK (trade_id, order_id)
        note right of OS: duplicate key = replay, counted not applied
        OS->>DB: PARTIALLY_FILLED or FILLED + audit row
        OS->>K: orders.lifecycle.v1
    and position-service applies the same fill
        K->>PS: trades.executed.v1
        PS->>PS: net quantity, exact open cost, realised P&L
    end

    C->>GW: GET /api/v1/orders/{id}
    GW->>OS: proxied request
    OS-->>C: order + fills + full audit trail
